From: Jernej Skrabec <jernej.skrabec@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 03:43:42 +0200
Subject: media: uapi: add MPEG-4 Part 2, H.263 and Sorenson
 Spark stateless decoder controls

Add a stateless decoder API for MPEG-4 Part 2 (the Simple and Advanced
Simple profiles of ISO/IEC 14496-2, which covers the DivX and Xvid
bitstreams), H.263 and Sorenson Spark.

There is one pixel format and one set of controls per syntax:

- V4L2_PIX_FMT_MPEG4_SLICE ('MG4S') carries one VOP, from its start code,
  with the V4L2_CID_STATELESS_MPEG4_VOL, _VOP and _QUANTISATION controls.

- V4L2_PIX_FMT_H263_SLICE ('S263') carries one H.263 picture, from its
  picture start code, with the V4L2_CID_STATELESS_H263_PICTURE control.
  MPEG-4 VOPs with a short video header are H.263 pictures.

- V4L2_PIX_FMT_SPK_SLICE ('SPKS') is the stateless counterpart of
  V4L2_PIX_FMT_SPK: the same picture control, with the version of the
  Sorenson Spark header.

The controls carry the syntax elements the decoding process needs, the
derived values a stateless decoder cannot compute without keeping state
across pictures (TRB/TRD of the direct mode, in frames and in fields)
and the references as capture buffer timestamps. Tools outside of the
Simple and Advanced Simple profiles (shapes, static sprites, scalability,
NEWPRED, reduced resolution VOPs, ...) are left out rather than added as
flags that every driver would have to refuse.

Hardware which cannot parse the video packet headers of MPEG-4 or the
GOB and slice headers of H.263 gets their location, macroblock number
and quantiser from the optional V4L2_CID_STATELESS_MPEG4_SLICE_PARAMS
and V4L2_CID_STATELESS_H263_SLICE_PARAMS dynamic arrays, like the
V4L2_CID_STATELESS_VC1_SLICE_PARAMS control, so that the kernel never
parses the bitstream.

Widespread MPEG-4 encoders deviate from the standard in ways the
bitstream does not reveal; decoding their output as encoded needs to
reproduce the deviations, which applications detect from the encoder
version in the user data. V4L2_CID_STATELESS_MPEG4_QUIRKS selects them,
each with the arithmetic it changes, and its maximum tells applications
which ones the driver can reproduce, so that they can decode the other
bitstreams in software.

Signed-off-by: Jernej Skrabec <jernej.skrabec@gmail.com>
